        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "*Datorren* literally means \"that is coming\" — from the verb *etorri* you learned in Unit 12. *Datorren astean* = \"in the coming week\". English says \"next\", Basque says \"coming\"; the idea is the same."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Can, can't, have to, want to",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Euskara",
            "Pattern",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**nahi**",
              "verb + nahi + auxiliary",
              "Joan nahi dut.",
              "I want to go."
            ],
            [
              "**behar**",
              "verb + behar + auxiliary",
              "Joan behar dut.",
              "I have to go."
            ],
            [
              "**ahal**",
              "verb + ahal + auxiliary",
              "Joan ahal dut.",
              "I can go."
            ],
            [
              "**ezin**",
              "ezin + verb + auxiliary",
              "Ezin dut joan.",
              "I can't go."
            ],
            [
              "**gogo**",
              "verb + gogoa + auxiliary",
              "Joateko gogoa dut.",
              "I really want to go."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The first four use the dictionary form of the verb, and the auxiliary always comes last. Note that *ezin* breaks the pattern: it goes **at the front** of the whole sentence, and the auxiliary follows right after it — just like *ez*."
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Euskara",
            "English"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Bihar lan egin behar dut.",
              "I have to work tomorrow."
            ],
            [
              "Gaur ezin dut etorri.",
              "I can't come today."
            ],
            [
              "Euskaraz hitz egin nahi dut.",
              "I want to speak Basque."
            ],
            [
              "Lagundu ahal didazu?",
              "Can you help me?"
            ],
            [
              "Ez dut joan nahi.",
              "I don't want to go."
            ],
            [
              "Zer egin behar dugu orain?",
              "What do we have to do now?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Ready-to-use plan sentences",
          "items": [
            "*Datorren astean Donostiara joango naiz.* — Next week I'll go to Donostia.",
            "*Udan Indonesiara itzuliko naiz.* — This summer I'll go back to Indonesia.",
            "*Datorren urtean B1 maila lortu nahi dut.* — Next year I want to reach B1.",
            "*Gaur gauean ezin dut atera, ikasi behar dut.* — Tonight I can't go out; I have to study.",
            "*Agian bihar ikusiko dugu elkar.* — Maybe we'll see each other tomorrow."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
